  "description": "Tiger Woods signed a five-year, $40 million Nike deal in 1996 at age 20, and became golf's biggest earner.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Tiger Woods: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_Woods\n- CBS News: Tiger Inks The $100M Deal: https://www.cbsnews.com/news/tiger-inks-the-100m-deal/\n- NBC Washington: Tiger Woods joins Michael Jordan, LeBron James as third athlete with net worth over $1 billion: https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/sports/tiger-woods-joins-michael-jordan-lebron-james-as-third-athlete-with-net-worth-over-1-billion/\n\nFrom the cited pages: in 1978 he putted against Bob Hope on TV as a toddler; Woods turned pro at 20 in August 1996 and signed with Nike (five years, $40 million); he won the 1997 Masters by 12 strokes at 21, the youngest winner; in 2000 he signed a 5-year, $105 million Nike extension, the largest endorsement package by a pro athlete at that time; in 2009 Forbes confirmed he was the first pro athlete to earn over a billion dollars in his career; less than 10% of his earnings come from prize money (NBC Washington, 2022 Forbes report). Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #tigerwoods #golf #howtheymakemoney",
